# Submit Lean for independent verification

Import LeanWebContract from "../src/lean_web_contract.lg".

Submission keeps one exact body after the first send. Retrying a lost response
uses that body and request key again. The server owns authorization and state.

## Page /lean
State:
    Let source be "".
    Let target be "".
    Let error be "".
    Let profile be "Loading verification profile…".
    Let ready be false.
    Let pending be false.
    Let locked be false.
    Let body be "".
    Let context be a new LeanSubmitContext with csrf "" and key "" and assignment "" and version 0 and profile "".
Actions:
    When the page loads:
        Get "/api/lean/context" as LeanSubmitContext, then initialized.
    To initialized (answer: Result of LeanSubmitContext and HttpError):
        Inspect answer:
            When Ok (value):
                Set context to value.
                Set profile to value's profile.
                Set ready to true.
            When Err (e):
                Set error to e's message.
                Set profile to "Verification profile unavailable".
    To submit:
        If pending or ready is equal to false:
            Return.
        If trim(source) is equal to "" or trim(target) is equal to "":
            Set error to "Enter Lean source and the declaration to verify.".
            Return.
        If locked is equal to false:
            Set body to leanSubmitBody(context, source, target).
            Set locked to true.
        Set pending to true.
        Set error to "".
        Post body to "/api/lean/jobs" as LeanAcceptedJob, then accepted.
    To accepted (answer: Result of LeanAcceptedJob and HttpError):
        Set pending to false.
        Inspect answer:
            When Ok (job):
                Navigate to "/lean/jobs/" + urlEncode(job's id).
            When Err (e):
                Set error to e's message.
View:
    <main>
      <h1>Verify Lean in LOGOS</h1>
      <p id="profile">{profile}</p>
      <p>Submit a declaration, download its LOGOS source and proof package, and replay the verification independently.</p>
      <form id="lean-submit" on-submit.prevent={submit}>
        <label for="source">Lean source</label>
        <textarea id="source" rows="16" bind={source} readonly={locked}></textarea>
        <label for="target">Declaration name</label>
        <input id="target" bind={target} readonly={locked}>
        <button id="submit" type="submit" disabled={pending or ready is equal to false}>Submit for verification</button>
      </form>
      {if pending:}<p role="status">Submitting…</p>{end}
      {if error is not "":}<p id="error" role="alert">{error}</p>{end}
      {if locked:}<p>Retries send the same source, declaration, and request key.</p>{end}
    </main>
Style:
    main { max-width: 52rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 1rem; color: #172033; background: #fff; }
    form { display: grid; gap: .75rem; }
    textarea, input, button { font: inherit; padding: .75rem; }
    textarea { font-family: monospace; resize: vertical; }
    [role="alert"] { color: #a01422; }
    :focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #2457c5; outline-offset: 3px; }

## Test: Lean form rejects an empty declaration without clearing source
Given that GET "/api/lean/context" answers 200 with "{{\"csrf\":\"test\",\"key\":\"one\",\"assignment\":\"a\",\"version\":1,\"profile\":\"Lean 4.14 core\"}}".
Type "theorem example : True := True.intro" into "#source".
Submit "#lean-submit".
Expect that the text of "#error" is equal to "Enter Lean source and the declaration to verify.".
Expect that the value of "#source" is equal to "theorem example : True := True.intro".

## Test: Lean form navigates only after the server accepts the job
Given that GET "/api/lean/context" answers 200 with "{{\"csrf\":\"test\",\"key\":\"two\",\"assignment\":\"a\",\"version\":1,\"profile\":\"Lean 4.14 core\"}}".
Given that POST "/api/lean/jobs" answers 200 with "{{\"id\":\"job-1\"}}".
Type "theorem example : True := True.intro" into "#source".
Type "example" into "#target".
Submit "#lean-submit".
Expect that the URL is equal to "/lean/jobs/job-1".

## Test: Lean form retains the submitted source when the server denies it
Given that GET "/api/lean/context" answers 200 with "{{\"csrf\":\"test\",\"key\":\"three\",\"assignment\":\"a\",\"version\":1,\"profile\":\"Lean 4.14 core\"}}".
Given that POST "/api/lean/jobs" answers 403 with "denied".
Type "theorem example : True := True.intro" into "#source".
Type "example" into "#target".
Submit "#lean-submit".
Expect that the count of "#error" is equal to 1.
Expect that the value of "#source" is equal to "theorem example : True := True.intro".
